    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0092" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.852/60: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tampico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Collins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-02T12:00:00-06:00">December 2,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A contact reports that the first officer of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Orinoco</hi> yesterday informed him that negotiations are in progress for
                    sale of the German vessels at Tampico to American interests and that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Orinoco’s</hi> captain and chief engineer are at Mexico
                    City or Villa Acuna Coahuila in this connection.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Collins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
